ASML Research offers various internship opportunities. Your internship may be more theoretical (analytical / numerical) or experimental, depending on your preferences. You will work in a multidisciplinary team of experts with access to experimental setups, where theoretical insights can be explored in practice. During your internship assignment, you may work on one or more of the topics below:

Apply your theoretical knowledge to optimize properties of optical systems and photonics;

Explore novel optical metrology concepts; 

Investigate new light sources and detectors;

Develop analytical and/or numerical physical models to understand the behaviour of advanced light sources;

Design and conduct experiments, interpret results and communicate findings;

Support setup automations to enable efficient measurements;

Design integrated photonic devices using commercial design software;

We offer Master's apprentice or thesis internships, requiring a commitment of 4-5 days a week, with a duration of 5 to 12 months. The internship content, start date and duration can be discussed during the interview. ASML provides internship compensation and if you receive an offer, you will be informed about it.

